# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  TEMPLATE ONLY — THIS FILE IS COMMITTED TO GIT.
#  A password typed here gets pushed. Do not put one here.
#
#  Copy it first, then edit the COPY:
#      PowerShell   copy .env.example .env
#      bash         cp .env.example .env
#
#  .env is git-ignored, and run_extract.py reads .env — never this file.
#  So filling this one in does not even work; it only leaks.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Anything already set in the environment wins over .env, so a one-off
#   $env:FUSION_PASSWORD = "..."
# still overrides it for that run.

